因为我们四面八方都面临着敌人。

168
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:24,460
Virginia to one side, Maryland to the other,
弗吉尼亚在一边，马里兰在另一边，

169
00:09:24,460 --> 00:09:25,960
which technically was part of the North,
从技术上讲属于北方，

170
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:28,040
but Maryland was very much Confederate-leaning.
但马里兰却极度倾向南方。

171
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:30,280
And then beyond that, we get refugees,
然后，我们还看到难民，那些曾被奴役的人，逃离了。

172
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:32,040
people formerly enslaved people,
曾经被奴役的人，

173
00:09:32,040 --> 00:09:33,120
fleeing their enslavers,
逃离他们的主人，

174
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:36,800
moving north to build a light for themselves. DC is the furthest south of the northern city.
向北迁移，为自己建造家园。华盛顿是北部城市中最南端的地方。

175
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:40,740
So this is where people were aiming to go. And then other folks either fleeing or coming
所以，人们原本是想前往这里。然后，其他人要么是逃离，要么是为战争而来。

176
00:09:40,740 --> 00:09:45,320
to profit from the war. So the population of Washington just explodes. So we go from
为了从战争中获利。因此，华盛顿的人口急剧膨胀。我们从

177
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:49,480
75,000 to 125,000 in four years.
5万增长到12.5万，仅用了四年。

178
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:56,200
But Hannah, we did not have the infrastructure to support this population explosion. And
但汉娜，我们并没有足够的基础设施来支撑这种人口激增。而且

179
00:09:56,200 --> 00:10:01,760
DC started to hit some pretty hard times. And so even as the Washington Monument is
华盛顿开始遭遇相当艰难的时期。而即使华盛顿纪念碑的建设进展缓慢，

