这些也同样被完全无视。

565
00:32:29,280 --> 00:32:32,680
I think people see it as a monument to the president,
我认为人们把它看作是为总统建立的纪念碑，

566
00:32:32,680 --> 00:32:35,740
a living president as a monument to ego
把一位在世的总统当作是为个人野心而立的纪念碑。

567
00:32:35,740 --> 00:32:39,200
and not as a real connection to the nation.
而不是与国家真正建立联系。

568
00:32:39,200 --> 00:32:41,240
I mean, the time at which the Roman Empire,
我说，罗马帝国时期，

569
00:32:41,240 --> 00:32:43,320
which is where triumphal arches come from,
那正是凯旋门的起源地，

570
00:32:43,320 --> 00:32:46,040
they were conquering, they were an empire,
他们是在征服，他们是一个帝国，

571
00:32:46,040 --> 00:32:48,420
They were not a democratic republic.
他们并非民主共和国。

572
00:32:48,420 --> 00:32:50,920
So that symbolism feels kind of incongruous,
所以这种象征意义显得很不协调，

573
00:32:50,920 --> 00:32:53,320
especially with the United States today.
尤其与当今的美国格格不入。

574
00:32:53,320 --> 00:32:55,140
There's also, of course, a financial component.
当然，还有财务方面的考量。

575
00:32:55,140 --> 00:32:56,300
Of course, people are like,
当然，人们会问，

576
